Our Why At Dotmatics&nbsp;

At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.

We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.

We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform - best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.

Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.

Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&nbsp;

Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.

You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.

We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&nbsp;

What do we need

We're looking for an IT Helpdesk Support Engineer/Technician to be the first line of technical support for employees across our multi-entity organization. You'll work in a hybrid identity environment (on-prem AD synced to Entra ID/Azure AD) alongside Google Workspace, supporting Windows and macOS users, and troubleshooting Exchange Online and Google Mail.&nbsp;
We currently have 2 open positions - these positions will work in shifts to support a global business, shift patterns may include working hours such as a split shit or early morning starts, your recruiter will give you more details.&nbsp;&nbsp;

In this role you will get to:

• Endpoints: Troubleshoot PC/Mac hardware, OS, and app issues; coordinate device replacement and deployment; support Intune/Jamf Pro policy and compliance&nbsp;

• Identity &amp; Access: Resolve login/auth issues across AD and Entra ID; process system and software access requests; support Google Workspace accounts&nbsp;

• Email: Troubleshoot Exchange Online and Google Mail issues; process DL and shared mailbox requests&nbsp;

• Network &amp; General Support: Basic Wi-Fi/VPN/connectivity troubleshooting; assist with change requests; handle general IT tickets&nbsp;

• Onboarding/Offboarding: Provision new hire access and devices; process offboarding (access revocation, device retrieval)&nbsp;

• Cloud Workspaces: Provision and troubleshoot AWS Workspaces for designated employees

• Ticketing: Own tickets in Jira Service Management (JSM) from intake to resolution within SLA; escalate as needed&nbsp;

We are looking for people who have 3-5 years in an IT helpdesk or desktop support role, working in a multi-geo environment supporting business users in multiple time zones and various productivity suites such as Microsoft and Google suites.&nbsp; You will have experience working UK &amp; US teams.&nbsp; This role requires a strong command of English both written and spoken.&nbsp;

The key skills we need&nbsp;

• Working tickets in Jira Service Management (JSM)&nbsp;

Liquid Personnel is recruiting an Adult Services Manager to join its client’s Adult Services leadership team, based in Coventry.

You will ensure adults and carers receive safe, effective, strengths-based, and person-centred support. Working closely with health partners, providers, community organisations, and internal stakeholders, you will promote independence, wellbeing, and community inclusion while overseeing performance, quality, resources, service development, workforce development, transformation, and continuous improvement across Adult Services.

What will your responsibilities be? &nbsp;

• Leading designated Adult Social Care service areas, ensuring safe, effective, strengths-based, and person-centred practice is consistently delivered.&nbsp;

• Providing operational leadership across Adult Services, working flexibly across service boundaries to support changing priorities and service demands.&nbsp;

• Supporting managers and practitioners through visible leadership, professional challenge, coaching, and the promotion of high-quality practice.

• Using performance data, management information, quality assurance findings, and customer feedback to drive service improvement and evidence outcomes.&nbsp;

• Monitoring risk, demand, service performance, and workforce capacity to ensure effective and safe service delivery.&nbsp;

• Contributing to strategic planning, workforce resilience, service transformation, and financial sustainability across Adult Social Care.&nbsp;

• Supporting the implementation and embedding of digital solutions and service transformation programmes to improve efficiency and outcomes.&nbsp;

• Working collaboratively with health partners, providers, community organisations, and stakeholders to strengthen integrated service delivery and improve outcomes for adults and carers.&nbsp;

• Promoting a positive practice culture that encourages accountability, innovation, learning, and continuous professional development.&nbsp;

• Leading on service development initiatives, quality assurance activity, and operational improvement programmes.

• Supporting resource management, budget oversight, and the delivery of value-for-money services.

• Acting as a constructive critical friend across Adult Services, supporting colleagues through challenge, shared learning, and collaborative problem-solving.&nbsp;

Qualifications and Experience: &nbsp;

To be successful in this role you must have; &nbsp;

• Relevant professional qualification in Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Health &amp; Social Care, Management, or a related field.

• Registration with the appropriate professional body where applicable.

• Significant management and leadership experience within Adult Social Care services.

• Proven experience leading operational teams, managing performance, and driving service improvement.

• Strong understanding of Adult Social Care legislation, safeguarding responsibilities, strengths-based practice, and person-centred approaches.

• Experience working collaboratively with health partners, providers, community organisations, and multi-agency stakeholders.

• Knowledge of workforce development, performance management, quality assurance, and service transformation.

• Experience using performance data and quality measures to inform decision-making and improve outcomes.

• Excellent leadership, communication, organisational, and stakeholder management skills.

• Ability to work effectively within a complex and changing service environment whilst maintaining a focus on positive outcomes for adults and carers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

